# Environment variables for this repository.
#
# There is nothing to copy to the repository root: no script, no build and no
# Vite/Astro config in the workspace reads a `.env` at this level. The two apps
# each read their own, resolved relative to the app directory, so a root `.env`
# would be silently ignored — which is worse than having none, because it looks
# like it is working.
#
# Use the per-app files instead:
#
#   cp apps/docs/.env.example apps/docs/.env
#   cp apps/demo/.env.example apps/demo/.env
#
# Both are identical today because both apps read the same three variables with
# the same defaults, but they are separate files on purpose: the apps deploy
# separately, and a docs-only override must not be forced on the demo build.
#
# Every value is OPTIONAL. A fresh clone builds, tests and runs with no `.env`
# at all — the defaults below are the values that were hardcoded before these
# variables existed. Set one only when a deploy genuinely needs to differ: a
# fork, a preview deployment, a staging docs site.
#
# Trailing slashes are stripped on read, so both forms work.
#
# The `PUBLIC_` prefix is Astro's marker for values that reach the browser
# bundle. It is not a secret marker, and nothing sensitive belongs in a `.env`
# here.

# The GitHub repository, without a trailing slash. Drives the repo links in the
# header, the footer and the demo catalog, and `repoFileUrl()`.
# Default: https://github.com/ailuracollective/alpinejs-toolkit
# PUBLIC_REPO_URL=

# The docs site. In apps/docs this is what ends up in `site:`, the canonical
# URLs and the sitemap, so a wrong value is the one mistake here that is not
# merely cosmetic.
# Default: https://ailuracollective.github.io/alpinejs-toolkit
# PUBLIC_DOCS_URL=

# The demo site.
# Default: https://ailura.dev
# PUBLIC_DEMO_URL=
